    "done_when": "packages/imas-alambic/install/imasdb.sh sets permissions under IMASDB with chmod -R o=rX, so on intr26-2 stat shows others r-x on IMASDB/bin/imas-alambic and on the managed python3.12 and r-- on non-executable files, and find IMASDB -not -type l -perm -o+w prints nothing. Both uv calls keep --no-cache, and uv python install runs with --no-bin so nothing lands in the installing account ~/.local/bin. imas-alambic config reports every setting even when no bundle is reachable: the machine and cache settings carry the discovery refusal as their source with no value instead of raising, pinned by a test in packages/imas-alambic/tests/test_settings.py, while write still refuses a missing machine. The installer then reads the layout names from config before the bundle exists and no longer seeds maps/current itself. The installer is rerun on intr26-2 through ssh jt-60sa, its gate log under the run directory names the revision it ran at in its header and ends with an EXIT= line, and every earlier check still passes: 1755 account directory, wheel not editable, --version with and without PYTHONPATH, uv pip check, config reporting IMASDB/maps/current, IMASDB/ids and jt-60sa. Separately, on intr26-2, the stray symlink /home/d240044/.local/bin/python3.12 created on 2026-10-07 is listed with ls -la, then removed, and the removal is printed; the directory it points to under /home/d240044/.local/share/uv/python is removed the same way only if its own mtime is 2026-10-07; nothing else under /home/d240044/.local is touched. uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests packages exits 0.",
